# Pose manifest for the terrain fill-tag sweep (tests/freecam/fill_sweep.py).
# One pose per line: level | x,y,z,yaw,pitch | tag
#   pose "default" = the canonical load-in camera (no freecam engaged).
# Optional 4th field: capture frame (default 2101) — for levels that load late.
#
# Selection rule: canonical-plausible cameras (the load-in view, gameplay-like
# views, plus the validated gapfill/freecam corpus spots). The og legs are only
# valid ground truth where the .s occlusion/culling verdicts fire for cameras
# the game could plausibly have; fully detached orbits under-cover in og and
# can only ADD candidate faces via views the game never shows — the review
# tier and the stencil gate bound that risk, but prefer plausible poses.
#
# Ordering matters for the marginal-new-faces curve: the harness processes
# poses in file order and reports how many new faces each pose contributes,
# per level — convergence is REGION-driven (adjacent poses add ~0), so grow
# this file by adding REGIONS, not orbit density.

